            "text": "Use CSS with the `:hover` pseudo-class:\n\n```html\n<span class=\"hover-color\">Hover over me</span>\n```\n\n```css\n.hover-color:hover {\n  color: red;\n}\n```\n\nYou can also do it inline with a `<style>` block:\n\n```html\n<style>\n  span:hover {\n    color: red;\n  }\n</style>\n\n<span>Hover over me</span>\n```\n\nIf you only want one specific `<span>` to change color, use a class or ID:\n\n```html\n<style>\n  #mySpan:hover {\n    color: blue;\n  }\n</style>\n\n<span id=\"mySpan\">Hover over me</span>\n```",
